## 7. Entry and Exit Criteria

All thresholds in this section are **proposed** and require agreement with the QA lead and product/bank owner.

### Entry Criteria

- Login scope, acceptance criteria, and applicable authentication policies are reviewed and approved.
- Test environment URL and supported platform matrix are documented.
- Environment is reachable, and a QA smoke check confirms the login page can be opened.
- At least one approved valid synthetic test account and the required negative test data are available.
- Test cases are reviewed; 100% of approved in-scope scenarios have defined preconditions and observable expected results.
- Defect logging, escalation contacts, and triage ownership are agreed.

### Exit Criteria

- 100% of approved in-scope login test cases have an execution result recorded.
- All failed cases have linked defects or a documented, approved disposition.
- No unresolved Severity 1 or Severity 2 defect remains in the in-scope login function, unless formally accepted by the designated business owner.
- The proposed pass threshold is at least 95% of executed in-scope cases passing; any lower result requires documented risk acceptance. This threshold is not a supplied bank criterion.
- Policy-dependent cases (for example, lockout/CAPTCHA) are either tested against approved requirements or explicitly recorded as not tested/out of scope for the cycle.
- QA lead and product/bank owner review the test summary and record a go/no-go recommendation.

